# GreenBoost Gaming Suite , udev rule
#
# greenboost.ko ships its `gaming_mode` module parameter as root-only
# (module_param(gaming_mode, int, 0644) in greenboost.c , see the sibling
# greenboost repo). GreenBoost Proton (greenboost_proton/proton) writes this
# parameter as the invoking (non-root) user to tell the kernel module a game
# is active, so inference T2 buffers get evicted ahead of gaming VRAM. Without
# group write access that write always fails silently.
#
# Scoped to the 'greenboost' group (created by install.sh), not world-writable.
#
# Fires when the module loads. For a module already loaded at install time,
# see greenboost-gaming.tmpfiles.conf, which covers that case once at boot
# (and install.sh applies both immediately, no reboot required).
#
# Install to: /etc/udev/rules.d/99-greenboost-gaming.rules

# The TEST guard is required: /etc/udev/rules.d is copied into the dracut
# initramfs, where udev evaluates this rule but coreutils does not exist. Without
# it, every boot logs two errors at ~1.9s ("greenboost: Failed to find and pin
# callout binary /bin/chgrp: No such file or directory"). The real-root
# systemd-tmpfiles pass applies the ownership anyway, so skipping in the
# initramfs costs nothing. Paths are /usr/bin, not /bin: udev pins the callout
# binary by real path.
SUBSYSTEM=="module", KERNEL=="greenboost", ACTION=="add", \
    TEST=="/usr/bin/chgrp", \
    RUN+="/usr/bin/chgrp greenboost /sys/module/greenboost/parameters/gaming_mode", \
    RUN+="/usr/bin/chmod 0664 /sys/module/greenboost/parameters/gaming_mode"
